/-
# Seed-generated components of the global physical face-strand graph

The literal corrected-slab fusion assignment already supplies a finite list
of edges between physical face-strand copies.  This module performs the next
mathematical contraction: symmetrize that edge list as a Boolean adjacency,
select the constructive rooted component of one explicit seed, and use
component closure to prove that its characteristic function is closed under
every local physical strand partner.

The seed is retained as `Type`-level data together with literal membership in
the endpoint carrier.  No existence is inferred by choice.  Every local
partner edge is proved to occur in the global assignment list, so partner
closure is a theorem about the same physical graph rather than an assumed
field.

Honest scope: this module constructs the seed component and its linkwise
partner-closed selections.  It does not yet prove that the compiled drop on a
physical face equals the target external-label change, assemble all lowered
auxiliary witnesses, or bound inverse component encodings.

Constructive contract: finite lists, decidable equality, and the existing
constructive rooted-component compiler only.  No `Classical.*`, choice,
`native_decide`, `sorry`, custom axiom, noncomputable declaration, or enlarged
heartbeat budget.
-/

